Lucciola: leave PAM's bare password prompt off the status line

The greeter writes each PAM prompt on the status line, so without a
fingerprint reader the login screen reads "Password:" under a field
whose placeholder already says "Type password". When PAM asks for a
secret with just its generic prompt, Linux-PAM's "Password: " (pam_unix
and most modules ask with it) in any case, or one of its translations
in Linux-PAM 1.7's catalogs (greetd's locale picks it), the greeter
does not write it: the status line stays as it is when a PAM message of
the same conversation is on it, and is cleared otherwise, so nothing
from an earlier conversation (another user's fingerprint prompt) is
left there. Any other prompt ("Password for ...:", "Verification
code:", another module's question) still shows, and so do 0002's own
texts ("Type the password, or Enter for the fingerprint" after the
reader gives up).

Applied by lucciola/greeter/noctalia-greeter.spec to the v1.6.0 tag,
after 0003. Could be proposed upstream (noctalia-dev/noctalia-greeter),
together with 0002, whose code it touches.

--- a/src/greeter/greeter_surface.cpp
+++ b/src/greeter/greeter_surface.cpp
@@ -90,6 +90,51 @@ namespace {
     return lower.find("finger") != std::string::npos;
   }
 
+  // PAM's generic password prompt: Linux-PAM's "Password: ", which pam_unix
+  // and most modules ask with, in English or in a translation from
+  // Linux-PAM 1.7's catalogs (greetd's locale picks it). Compared without
+  // the spaces around it and the colon at its end, ASCII letters in any
+  // case. "Password for ...:", "Verification code:" and the like are not.
+  bool isGenericPasswordPrompt(std::string_view text) {
+    static constexpr std::string_view kGeneric[] = {
+      "adgangskode", "contrasenya", "contrasigno", "focal faire", "geslo", "heslo", "iphasiwedi",
+      "kata sandi", "lozinka", "mot de passe", "palavra-passe", "parola", "parool", "pasahitza",
+      "passord", "password", "passwort", "pasvorto", "salasana", "senha", "wachtwoord",
+      "contraseña", "hasło", "jelszó", "lösenord", "mật khẩu", "Şifrə", "Κωδικός πρόσβασης",
+      "Лозинка", "Парола", "Пароль", "ססמה", "كلمة السر", "गुप्तशब्द", "शब्दकूट", "গুপ্তশব্দ",
+      "পাসওয়ার্ড", "ਪਾਸਵਰਡ", "પાસવર્ડ", "ପ୍ରବେଶ ସଙ୍କେତ", "கடவுச்சொல்", "సంకేతపదము", "ಗುಪ್ತಪದ",
+      "അടയാളവാക്ക്", "රහස්පදය", "პაროლი", "ពាក្យសម្ងាត់", "パスワード", "密码", "密碼", "비밀번호",
+    };
+    // Spaces, and the no-break space some translations put before the colon.
+    const auto trim = [](std::string_view s, bool front) {
+      for (;;) {
+        if (s.empty()) {
+          return s;
+        }
+        if (!front && s.ends_with("\xc2\xa0")) {
+          s.remove_suffix(2);
+        } else if (std::isspace(static_cast<unsigned char>(front ? s.front() : s.back())) != 0) {
+          front ? s.remove_prefix(1) : s.remove_suffix(1);
+        } else {
+          return s;
+        }
+      }
+    };
+    std::string_view word = trim(trim(text, true), false);
+    // ":", the full-width colon (Chinese) or the Khmer one.
+    for (const std::string_view colon : {":", "\xef\xbc\x9a", "\xe1\x9f\x96"}) {
+      if (word.ends_with(colon)) {
+        word.remove_suffix(colon.size());
+        break;
+      }
+    }
+    std::string lower(trim(word, false));
+    std::ranges::transform(lower, lower.begin(), [](unsigned char c) {
+      return c < 0x80 ? static_cast<char>(std::tolower(c)) : static_cast<char>(c);
+    });
+    return std::ranges::find(kGeneric, std::string_view(lower)) != std::end(kGeneric);
+  }
+
